<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Javelin</h1>
<p>Average Length: 6 feet.
Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-Hand.
Commonly used by: Several classes.
</p><p>Javelins were often all wooden, with either one or both ends sharpened. They could be used for throwing, or hand-to-hand combat. They weren't great weapons, but their length and versatility made them valuable.
</p><p>The javelin thus was a short, light weight spear designed solely to be thrown. Some were constructed entirely of metal but most were metal spear tips mounted on a wooden shaft. Often a throwing device would also be used to increase the range and force of the javelin. There is no one particular design or example of what a javelin was; any short spear used for throwing was called a javelin. The javelin was used throughout history, most effectively by the ancient Greeks. One example is the jarid, a Turkish all-steel short javelin.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the javelin is a weapon skill of its own, one of the polearms (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it pierces, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is of middling speed. No guild teaches it, but anyone may throw one (see <a cmd='#'>Help Throw</a>).
</p><p><br />
